Below is an example of a complete React component for a shopping cart using Redux Toolkit for state management. This example will include a `Container` component where the cart is displayed, and a `CartProduct` component to represent each product in the cart.

First, ensure you have Redux Toolkit and React Redux installed. If not, run `npm install @reduxjs/toolkit react-redux` in your project.

### Step 1: Setup Redux Toolkit

In your root directory, create a file named `features/cart/cartSlice.js` and add the following code for the cart state management:

```javascript
import { createSlice } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';

const initialState = {
  items: [],
  totalQuantity: 0,
};

const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'cart',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    addItem(state, action) {
      const existingItem = state.items.find((item) => item.id === action.payload.id);
      if (existingItem) {
        existingItem.quantity += action.payload.quantity;
      } else {
        state.items.push(action.payload);
      }
      state.totalQuantity += action.payload.quantity;
    },
    removeItem(state, action) {
      state.items = state.items.filter((item) => item.id!== action.payload);
      state.totalQuantity -= action.payload.quantity;
    },
  },
});

export const { addItem, removeItem } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

This slice manages the cart items and the total quantity.

### Step 2: Store Setup

Create a store in `store/index.js`:

```javascript
import { configureStore } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import cartReducer from '../features/cart/cartSlice';

export default configureStore({
  reducer: {
    cart: cartReducer,
  },
});
```

